{"report":"Implemented the progress fix in src/progress.js. The watcher now subscribes before feed.start(), restoring synchronous cached initial progress. It assigns source-arrival order to frames: every decoded frame still calls recordProgress, while showProgress only accepts frames newer than the latest displayed one, preventing async decode reordering from rolling the panel back.

Verified with /runtime/node v16.20.2:
- cached initial packet reaches history and panel;
- reversed async decode completion records both frames but preserves newer panel state;
- ordinary live streaming works;
- diagnostic telemetry continues to skip cached bootstrap and receive live packets;
- retry, selection/navigation, hide/dispose cleanup, cancellation, queue records, notices, and progress records retain expected behavior.

Archived the standalone unified patch at /workspace/patch-archive/initial-progress-ordering.patch. No external/full test suite was present or run."}
